      {
        "t": "mistake",
        "html": "<b>pan-</b> means “all” only in words from Greek (<i>panorama</i>, <i>panacea</i>, <i>pandemonium</i>). A <i>pancake</i> is cooked in a pan and a <i>panel</i> is a flat board: neither has anything to do with “all.”"
      },
      {
        "t": "note",
        "html": "Two words with stories. <b>Bus</b> is short for <i>omnibus</i>, a Latin word meaning “for all”: a carriage anyone could ride. And <b>pandemonium</b> was made up by an English poet for a crowded, noisy capital of spirits in a long poem (<i>pan-</i>, all + <i>demon</i>, spirit). Today it means any wild uproar."
      },
